  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "mostlylucid.Markdig.FetchExtension v1.0.0\n=========================================\n\nInitial release of the Markdig Fetch Extension - enables fetching and embedding remote\nMarkdown content at render time with smart caching.\n\nKEY FEATURES\n------------\n\n* Simple inline syntax: <fetch markdownurl=\"URL\" pollfrequency=\"24h\"/>\n* Multiple storage backends: In-Memory, File-based, and custom implementations\n* Smart caching with configurable poll frequency (hours)\n* Stale-while-revalidate pattern: Returns cached content if fetch fails\n* Link transformation: Automatically rewrites relative links to absolute URLs\n* Fetch metadata summaries: Display when content was last fetched\n* Flexible template system for metadata display\n* Full dependency injection support\n* Thread-safe operations across all storage providers\n* Preprocessing architecture ensures fetched content flows through your entire\n  Markdig pipeline with all custom extensions\n\nSTORAGE OPTIONS\n---------------\n\n* In-Memory: Perfect for demos, testing, simple apps (no persistence)\n* File-Based: Single-server production with disk persistence\n* Database Plugins: SQLite, PostgreSQL, SQL Server (separate packages)\n* Custom: Implement IMarkdownFetchService for specialized needs\n\nUSAGE EXAMPLE\n-------------\n\nservices.AddInMemoryMarkdownFetch();\nFetchMarkdownExtension.ConfigureServiceProvider(serviceProvider);\nvar pipeline = new MarkdownPipelineBuilder()\n    .UseAdvancedExtensions()\n    .Use<FetchMarkdownExtension>()\n    .Build();\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n------------\n\n* .NET 9.0+\n* Markdig 0.42.0+\n* Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection 9.0+\n\nDOCUMENTATION\n-------------\n\nFull documentation: https://github.com/scottgal/mostlylucidweb/tree/main/Mostlylucid.Markdig.FetchExtension\nIntegration guide: See INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md in the repository\n\nLICENSE\n-------\n\nUnlicense (public domain)",
